    html: |-
      <div>
                  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How to tell ADHD apart from typical child development</h2>
                  <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Not every energetic child has ADHD. These questions can help you distinguish:</p>
                  <ul class="space-y-3">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Are the symptoms visible in <strong class="text-ink">more than one setting</strong> — both at home and at school?</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Are the behaviours negatively affecting the child's <strong class="text-ink">academic performance, friendships or self-esteem</strong>?</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Has this been going on <strong class="text-ink">consistently for at least six months</strong>?</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Are these behaviours <strong class="text-ink">noticeably more intense than in peers</strong> of the same age?</p>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                  <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-4">If you answer "yes" to most of these, it is worth speaking with a specialist.</p>
                </div>
  - type: ozel
    html: |-
      <div>
                  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How does the assessment process work?</h2>
                  <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">An ADHD diagnosis is not based on a single test. A thorough evaluation typically involves:</p>
                  <ul class="space-y-3">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">1</div>
                      <div>
                        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Clinical interviews</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Separate interviews with the child and parents covering developmental history, school performance and family dynamics.</p>
                      </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">2</div>
                      <div>
                        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Parent and teacher rating scales</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Standardised rating scales used by the psychologist measure symptom severity across different settings.</p>
                      </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">3</div>
                      <div>
                        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Psychological testing</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Tests measuring attention, memory and executive functions help distinguish ADHD from learning difficulties, anxiety or other conditions.</p>
                      </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">4</div>
                      <div>
                        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Medical evaluation</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Medical causes of similar symptoms — such as hearing difficulties, thyroid problems or sleep disorders — are ruled out.</p>
                      </div>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
  - type: onayli-liste
    baslik: Treatment and support options
    giris: 'ADHD is a treatable condition. The most effective approach combines more than one strategy:'
    maddeler:
      - baslik: Behavioural Therapy
        aciklama: The first-line choice, particularly for children under 6. It teaches the child self-regulation skills and helps parents build consistent structure at home.
      - baslik: Parent Training
        aciklama: Expert guidance on communication strategies, reward systems and home routines. Research shows that parent training is as effective as direct child therapy for many families.
      - baslik: Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)
        aciklama: Particularly helpful for school-age children and adolescents. Addresses organisation, time management and unhelpful thinking patterns.
      - baslik: School Accommodations
        aciklama: Extended time in exams, a front-row seat, homework tracking tools — reasonable adjustments that can significantly improve academic outcomes.
      - baslik: Medication
        aciklama: Prescribed by a psychiatrist after full evaluation. For moderate to severe presentations, stimulant or non-stimulant medication combined with behavioural support can produce meaningful results.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: turuncu
    baslik: Why early support matters
    metin: Children who grow up without a diagnosis are sometimes labelled "lazy", "disrespectful" or "a failure". These labels erode self-confidence and increase the risk of secondary [anxiety](/en/blog/what-is-anxiety-disorder.html) or [depression](/en/blog/what-is-depression.html). Early intervention can break that cycle and bring the child's strengths to the fore.
